d after the later restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-dd137540a5814193\",\"cmd-881b1caf7fbf407c\",\"cmd-15d914f9d2194a89\",\"cmd-60ee2b8db961491a\"]},{\"id\":\"update-skips-curl\",\"requirement\":\"A system update leaves curl at its current version (does not upgrade it)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A dnf update simulation (tsflags=test) was run against the live repos; grepping the transaction output shows only libcurl (a distinct package) scheduled to upgrade while curl does not appear, and 'rpm -q curl' before and after the simulation remained curl-8.9.1-5.el10. This is a simulated transaction rather than a real applied update, but it directly demonstrates the versionlock mechanism excluding curl from the transaction set, the standard and expected verification method.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-881b1caf7fbf407c\",\"cmd-46fd22c9b2654ea8\"]},{\"id\":\"provider-restart-protocol-node1\",\"requirement\":\"Independent provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on node1: pre-restart healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered service/data state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart baseline captured boot_id d9f8550d-5cb3-4929-9e62-a388df86bcf6 with curl functional and versionlock active. 'sudo shutdown -r now' was issued and acknowledged; subsequent exec calls show connection timeouts/resets consistent with the node going down, then a successful reconnect. Post-restart capture shows a new boot_id c9eeaf65-2226-4750-9fb9-d7b56e9ebed4, curl still functional at the same version, and the versionlock entry intact. Corroborated by the fixed lifecycle before/after-executor boot-identity snapshots showing the identical transition independently.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-15d914f9d2194a89\",\"cmd-60372ccc607842f9\",\"cmd-5e488d2d9c954fba\",\"cmd-63f06b2bebea4e81\",\"cmd-460df4b3721348f5\",\"cmd-be8ba20855634cbe\",\"cmd-60ee2b8db961491a\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"All state-changing commands trace to a clear purpose: rpm --import of the redhat-release GPG key (cmd-dd137540a5814193) was a necessary prerequisite to unblock the versionlock plugin install, which itself (and its dependency upgrades to dnf-plugins-core/python3-dnf-plugins-core) was required to add the curl lock; the versionlock add is the core task action; the dnf update simulations (cmd-881b1caf7fbf407c, cmd-46fd22c9b2654ea8) used tsflags=test and made no persistent package changes, serving as bounded final verification; and the restart (cmd-60372ccc607842f9) was performed to satisfy the separate node-restart evidence protocol. The only residue is two small diagnostic log files left in /tmp (/tmp/reboot.log from the shutdown command's redirected output, and /tmp/versionlock_install.log from the initial failed install attempt) that were not cleaned up after use — low-risk, non-destructive leftovers rather than functional problems. No failed services, no unsafe exposure changes, and package-health checks remained clean before and after.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-dd137540a5814193\",\"cmd-4cb96b37437f474e\",\"cmd-60372ccc607842f9\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor installed the versionlock plugin (resolving a GPG import blocker), locked curl at its installed version 8.9.1-5.el10, and verified via a dnf update simulation that curl is excluded from update transactions while an unrelated package (libcurl) still upgrades. It then completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol on node1, capturing a healthy pre-restart baseline, a restart acknowledgement, a directly observed boot-identity change, and confirmation that curl's version and versionlock survived the reboot — corroborated by the fixed lifecycle boot-identity snapshots. Minor hygiene issue: two small log files were left in /tmp without cleanup, but no other unnecessary, broad, or destructive mutations occurred.\",\"limitations\":[\"The 'system update leaves curl at its current version' outcome was verified via a dnf test-mode (dry-run) transaction rather than a fully applied real update, so behavior under an actual completed update was not directly observed.\",\"Two diagnostic log files (/tmp/reboot.log, /tmp/versionlock_install.log) were left on node1 without cleanup; low-risk but unaddressed residue.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"versionlock-applied","requirement":"Install and apply a version lock on the curl package at its currently installed version on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"python3-dnf-plugin-versionlock was installed (after resolving a GPG key import blocker) and 'dnf versionlock add curl' locked curl-0:8.9.1-5.el10.*, confirmed by 'dnf versionlock list' output showing the entry both before and after the later restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dd137540a5814193","cmd-881b1caf7fbf407c","cmd-15d914f9d2194a89","cmd-60ee2b8db961491a"]},{"id":"update-skips-curl","requirement":"A system update leaves curl at its current version (does not upgrade it)","status":"satisfied","summary":"A dnf update simulation (tsflags=test) was run against the live repos; grepping the transaction output shows only libcurl (a distinct package) scheduled to upgrade while curl does not appear, and 'rpm -q curl' before and after the simulation remained curl-8.9.1-5.el10. This is a simulated transaction rather than a real applied update, but it directly demonstrates the versionlock mechanism excluding curl from the transaction set, the standard and expected verification method.","evidence_ids":["cmd-881b1caf7fbf407c","cmd-46fd22c9b2654ea8"]},{"id":"provider-restart-protocol-node1","requirement":"Independent provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on node1: pre-restart healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered service/data state","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart baseline captured boot_id d9f8550d-5cb3-4929-9e62-a388df86bcf6 with curl functional and versionlock active. 'sudo shutdown -r now' was issued and acknowledged; subsequent exec calls show connection timeouts/resets consistent with the node going down, then a successful reconnect. Post-restart capture shows a new boot_id c9eeaf65-2226-4750-9fb9-d7b56e9ebed4, curl still functional at the same version, and the versionlock entry intact. Corroborated by the fixed lifecycle before/after-executor boot-identity snapshots showing the identical transition independently.","evidence_ids":["cmd-15d914f9d2194a89","cmd-60372ccc607842f9","cmd-5e488d2d9c954fba","cmd-63f06b2bebea4e81","cmd-460df4b3721348f5","cmd-be8ba20855634cbe","cmd-60ee2b8db961491a","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.9,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.85,"summary":"All state-changing commands trace to a clear purpose: rpm --import of the redhat-release GPG key (cmd-dd137540a5814193) was a necessary prerequisite to unblock the versionlock plugin install, which itself (and its dependency upgrades to dnf-plugins-core/python3-dnf-plugins-core) was required to add the curl lock; the versionlock add is the core task action; the dnf update simulations (cmd-881b1caf7fbf407c, cmd-46fd22c9b2654ea8) used tsflags=test and made no persistent package changes, serving as bounded final verification; and the restart (cmd-60372ccc607842f9) was performed to satisfy the separate node-restart evidence protocol. The only residue is two small diagnostic log files left in /tmp (/tmp/reboot.log from the shutdown command's redirected output, and /tmp/versionlock_install.log from the initial failed install attempt) that were not cleaned up after use — low-risk, non-destructive leftovers rather than functional problems. No failed services, no unsafe exposure changes, and package-health checks remained clean before and after.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dd137540a5814193","cmd-4cb96b37437f474e","cmd-60372ccc607842f9","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The executor installed the versionlock plugin (resolving a GPG import blocker), locked curl at its installed version 8.9.1-5.el10, and verified via a dnf update simulation that curl is excluded from update transactions while an unrelated package (libcurl) still upgrades. It then completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol on node1, capturing a healthy pre-restart baseline, a restart acknowledgement, a directly observed boot-identity change, and confirmation that curl's version and versionlock survived the reboot — corroborated by the fixed lifecycle boot-identity snapshots. Minor hygiene issue: two small log files were left in /tmp without cleanup, but no other unnecessary, broad, or destructive mutations occurred.","limitations":["The 'system update leaves curl at its current version' outcome was verified via a dnf test-mode (dry-run) transaction rather than a fully applied real update, so behavior under an actual completed update was not directly observed.","Two diagnostic log files (/tmp/reboot.log, /tmp/versionlock_install.log) were left on node1 without cleanup; low-risk but unaddressed residue."]},"ttft_ms":19188,"type":"result","duration_ms":54757,"uuid":"051abb5f-eb33-4e35-9070-44b7aac2cf41","ttft_stream_ms":2180,"time_to_request_ms":187,"first_content_frame_ms":2180,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
